#<center>**Will-Based Estate Plan{[if IsGeauxMarriedTF]} for a Married Couple{[endif]}**</center>

The Will-Based Estate Plan includes a **Last Will and Testament**, a **Financial Power of Attorney**, and a **Medical Power of Attorney**, as well as an **Advanced Healthcare Directive** (a/k/a “Living Will”).  

{[if IsGeauxMarriedTF]}
Distributions to your spouse are either outright or in usufruct. 

{[endif]}
All bequests to your children (or other persons you select) can either be in trust or outright.

{[if isTheusTF]}
<center><img src="https://geauxplans.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/cropped-fav-300x300.png" alt="Geaux Shield - a blue and silver stylized shield icon" height="30" width="30"></center>
{[endif]}

{[if IsYouAppTF]}
If you want to name anyone not listed above in your documents, enter their information in this section. These can be people or entities. 

For example, you may want to have your niece serve as the Executor of your Will, and leave half of your estate to her and half to a charity. You would enter both your niece's information and the charity's information in this section as separate entries.
{[elseif GeauxPoATF]}
Enter the personal information about the people who will be designated as Financial or Healthcare Agents under any Power of Attorney created in your Power of Attorney Supplement.  

Be sure to include personal information for each initial agent, as well as any successor agent who would serve in the event the initial agent is unable or unwilling to serve or to continue to serve as Agent.  A successor Agent is not required if you only wish to appoint an initial Agent.
{[endif]}

*Please Note:  You can (and should) return to this section to add additional person(s) if you later decide you wish to appoint a person for a role and do not see them as an available choice from the drop-down menu.*

{[if isTheusTF]}
<center><img src="https://geauxplans.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/12/cropped-fav-300x300.png" alt="Geaux Shield - a blue and silver stylized shield icon" height="30" width="30"></center>
{[endif]}

